  "slug": "design-learning-9fdc",
  "summary": "Recent preprints and publications extend pretrained language models to embedding services, sequence design, codon optimization and viral genome analysis.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is the transfer of pretrained language models and Transformer architectures to biological sequence tasks, spanning prediction and design. Biocentral provides standardized web and API access to protein language model embeddings for prediction and training, demonstrated on the BFVD. Several items target nucleotide design: CodonTranslator, a 150M-parameter decoder-only Transformer trained on 62M CDS-protein pairs, conditions codon optimization on lineage and protein sequence; mRNABERT combines dual tokenization with protein-contrastive learning; codonGPT applies reinforcement learning to a generative model. ProtDAT designs protein sequences from text descriptions, and DeepSeek V3.2 generated 4-helix bundle sequences assessed by pLDDT and RMSD. Protein Set Transformer and Helixer extend the approach to viral genomes and gene models. What is new is the breadth of tasks addressed by language-model frameworks, though supporting evidence is largely benchmark-based.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2025-11-27"
}
